          "modules": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "<p><strong><strong>Sunjata The Musical!</strong></strong></p><p><em><strong><strong>A Celebration of West African History Through Dance, Music &amp; Storytelling.</strong></strong></em></p><p>Join a professional cast accompanied by our scholarship students on an exciting adventure from East London all the way to the legendary Mali Empire.</p><p>Take a trip back in time with us to discover Timbuktu, Mansa Musa, and the legendary lion king of Mali, Sunjata Keita!</p><p>Our amazing African artists will make the vibrant culture come alive with their captivating music, dance, and storytelling!</p><p>Learn the history of the great Mali Empire in West Africa and its founder 'Sunjata Keita'through this performance of African unity.</p><p>Our talented artists work extremely hard to prepare for each production and every special event.</p><p>Make sure you don’t miss out on any of our incredible performances by buying your tickets today.</p><p><em><strong><strong>Featuring a</strong></strong></em><em><strong><strong> collective of talented African artists, dancers, musicians, and storytellers, including artists from</strong></strong></em><em><strong><strong>T</strong></strong></em><em><strong><strong>uba Dance Theatre’s Scholarship Programme:</strong></strong></em></p><p>● Mohamed Kouyate – Artist &amp; Dancer</p><p>● Aboubacar Konte – Artist &amp; Musician</p><p>● Assita Sangara – Artist &amp; Singer</p><p>● Eddie Manu – Artist &amp; Dancer</p><p>● Oumy Mbaye – Artist &amp; Dancer</p><p>● Seydou Kienou – Artist &amp; Musician</p><p>● Ansumana Suso – Artist &amp; Musician</p><p>● Momo Momo – Artist &amp; Musician</p><p>● Fumy Fumzgop – Artist &amp; Dancer</p><p>● Yannick Mindu - Artist &amp; Dancer</p><p>● Brenda - Artist &amp; Dancer</p><p>● John-Samuel - Artist &amp; Actor</p><p><strong><strong>PLEASE SEE FAQ's FOR FURTHER INFORMATION INCLUDING ACCESSIBLE REQUIREMENTS</strong></strong></p>",
